WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.840
- My next guests are WWE Superstars

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:06.210
who are scheduled to be inducted
into the WWE Hall of Fame

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.930
this year, awesome!

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:10.470
They have a new book out
called "Incomparable"

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:13.240
and they're the stars of the
reality show "Total Bellas"

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:14.073
on E!

00:00:14.073 --> 00:00:15.670
Take a look.

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:16.700
- Are you guys ready?

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:18.060
- [Bearded Man] Yeah.
- [Woman] We're ready.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:22.683
- [Crowd] 10, nine, eight, seven, six,

00:00:22.683 --> 00:00:25.750
five, four, three, two, one.

00:00:27.303 --> 00:00:32.303
(crowd cheering)
(exciting music)

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:39.950
- All right, Brie and Nikki Bella,

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:41.050
are you there?

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:42.730
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:46.480
- Hi. Oh my gosh, y'all are
so beautiful, good gosh.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:49.680
You're actually goddesses,
and it's like...

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:51.550
Well it is lovely to meet y'all,

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.250
thank you so much for
hanging with me on my show.

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:57.230
And congrats, so to you both.

00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:59.770
Twins having babies at the same time,

00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:01.787
you obviously planned that?

00:01:01.787 --> 00:01:02.677
Like--

00:01:02.677 --> 00:01:04.530
- No, how crazy is that.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.650
- Wait, you didn't plan it?

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:07.483
- [Nikki] No.
- No.

00:01:07.483 --> 00:01:10.400
We actually both were
surprised by our pregnancies.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:13.150
- So, Brie found out first

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:15.080
and she was already set on one,

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:17.590
like she has a little girl
and it took her a while.

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:20.030
They tried for a while for baby number two

00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:21.276
and then they were just set like,

00:01:21.276 --> 00:01:22.870
we're meant to have one kid.

00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:25.440
And I had just gotten
engaged and I was like,

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:27.390
well, I'm not gonna have kids for years

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:28.670
and it'll probably be just one.

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:30.160
I'll be you know, in my 40s

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:31.193
and just do the one.

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:35.310
And then she came to me and
told me she was pregnant

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:36.540
and I was just so shocked

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:38.660
because I knew like, I was like,

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:39.980
were you guys trying?

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:42.060
Like, what was it?

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:44.530
And then two days later,
I started to feel symptoms

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:46.320
but I'm thinking it's my twin like

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:48.100
it's a twin thing.
- It's twin thing.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.710
- But I was like, I'm
just gonna take a test

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:53.030
and I saw positive and I
was like there is no way

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:54.950
and I took another test a week later

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:56.480
'cause then I was late

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:58.060
and we're a week and a 1/2 apart.

00:01:58.060 --> 00:01:59.900
- We're like, someone up there has a plan.

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:00.758
- Yeah.

00:02:00.758 --> 00:02:03.190
- A week and a 1/2 apart unplanned,

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:05.090
I mean I guess you can't
really plan it in general

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:06.180
'cause you never know
when that's gonna happen.

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:08.430
But that's insane.

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:09.263
- [Brie] Yeah.

00:02:09.263 --> 00:02:11.160
- I just never heard anything like that,

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:12.470
that's crazy.

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:14.800
- We literally just got
back from our doctors,

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.440
and you know, right now

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:18.220
because of everything,
you know, you have to,

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:20.900
your spouse can't come
with you or your loved one.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:22.700
But we're lucky that
we're pregnant together,

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:25.380
we get to go together so
our doctor always sees us

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:26.934
at the same time, we
do everything together.

00:02:26.934 --> 00:02:27.767
- Yeah.

00:02:27.767 --> 00:02:30.420
- Our baby had the exact
same heart rate today.

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:31.380
- What?

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:32.560
- I mean, it's weird.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:33.393
- Yeah.

00:02:33.393 --> 00:02:34.226
- It's like (mumbles).

00:02:34.226 --> 00:02:35.400
- It's the coolest thing.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:38.030
That's just such a cool
thing that does not happen

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:39.090
to anyone.

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:41.200
So, that's, I mean, it's already special

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.830
you're already twins, it's
just like double special.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.330
Brie, how did you keep, I mean,

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:46.710
'cause you also have a three year old,

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:49.050
like how did you keep your
three year old entertained?

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:51.980
I did see a photo of you
guys dressed as robots,

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:53.280
which was awesome.

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:55.570
- You know, it's funny because
I feel like all parents

00:02:55.570 --> 00:02:57.800
it's like, everyday my biggest challenge

00:02:57.800 --> 00:02:59.410
is keeping my toddler entertained

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:02.700
and at the same time I wanna
make her brain work, yeah.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:06.100
And so, she just kept
pointing at this robot

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:07.360
in this book.

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:09.200
And so I was like, you know what?

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:11.870
Right now we're all
getting so many boxes sent

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:14.220
to out front door, I should
just use these boxes,

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:18.145
use my leftover gift wrapping
and just make robots.

00:03:18.145 --> 00:03:18.978
- Yeah.

00:03:18.978 --> 00:03:21.210
- And I did and it was
actually really fun for me.

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:22.590
I did it during her nap time

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:24.680
and I actually was so into it.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:26.520
But now, we have a robot outfit

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:28.320
which just takes up
more space in the house,

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:29.580
but we love it.

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:31.000
We get in them and she...

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:34.760
- And what was so cute
is when she got in them,

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:36.960
she asked us like where is the popcorn?

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:38.750
- We're like, popcorn?

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:40.860
So I realized from the
book the robot always

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:42.760
has like held a popcorn.
- Always held popcorn.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:43.595
- So she's--

00:03:43.595 --> 00:03:45.340
- Yeah, you're like you
didn't nail this costume.

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:47.430
- Yeah. Where is popcorn mom, come on.

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:49.360
- Which is probably why
she likes the robot,

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:50.970
'cause she's like, wait, I get popcorn.

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:51.803
- Yeah.

00:03:51.803 --> 00:03:53.596
- [Kelly] (mumbles)
it's mac and ball, yeah.

00:03:53.596 --> 00:03:54.610
- You're smart.

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:56.130
- So Nikki, I mean, speaking of books

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:58.120
your new book, gets pretty deep

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:00.460
into your tough upbringing, right?

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:03.110
So was it hard to relive
some of those stories?

00:04:03.110 --> 00:04:04.820
I can't, you know, people
have always asked me

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:06.000
about writing a book about my life

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.950
and I'm just not there yet, like I just,

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:10.150
there is a lot of stuff I
think I'm working through.

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:11.573
Like, was that hard?

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:14.550
- It was definitely hard.

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:15.700
You know, for Brie and I,

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:17.150
we've been in and out of therapy

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:19.010
since we've been 15 years old.

00:04:19.010 --> 00:04:20.580
And...

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:23.640
But then we became apart
of the WWE universe

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:26.040
and then we're on reality TV

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:29.480
and we had this fandom
called the Bella Army.

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:31.040
And we became very intimate with them,

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.950
like, we were very inspired
and motivated by their stories

00:04:33.950 --> 00:04:35.510
and how they were motivated by us

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:38.440
and so when we were approached
about doing an autobiography,

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:39.920
we were like, well you know what?

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:41.780
If we do this, we want it to be a memoir

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:44.660
and we want it to be that when you close

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:47.110
that last page, that you
take something from it.

00:04:47.110 --> 00:04:49.360
That it's not just about our achievement

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:51.790
and just about life but
Brie and I go to a place

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:55.610
that, where people look at us as victims

00:04:55.610 --> 00:04:57.900
but how we truly, cause we had each other,

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:00.139
we made ourselves be survivors.

00:05:00.139 --> 00:05:03.340
And even you know, for
me, I shared a few stories

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:05.210
that I had never shared
even with my own mother.

00:05:05.210 --> 00:05:07.850
My mum didn't even know about
it till the book came out

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:11.090
because I still didn't have
the confidence to tell her

00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:13.000
that I was raped twice
in high school and--

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.640
- That is a really
rough thing for your mum

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:17.340
to probably hear to, you know, not know.

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:20.490
- She's, it was a very
emotional week for us

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:21.937
and it was like, even
when we wrote the book,

00:05:21.937 --> 00:05:25.050
it was like constant being back in therapy

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:26.550
but what I've realized is like

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:30.100
women and girls and even men and boys,

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:32.166
like they need those role models

00:05:32.166 --> 00:05:35.090
to be confident to talk about
what they're going through

00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:37.470
because what I've realized,
is when I've held on

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:39.490
to things for over 20 years,

00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:42.150
it doesn't help you grow as a human being.

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:44.960
And we really have to,
yeah, have that confidence

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:46.580
to speak out and that's
what Brie and I said.

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:48.150
We, let's put it all out there

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:50.010
because so many people
are gonna relate to this

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:53.050
and living in this filter
world of social media,

00:05:53.050 --> 00:05:54.980
people know that, need to know that

00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:56.040
there's people in the spotlight

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:57.850
that they could be like,
whoa, they went through that

00:05:57.850 --> 00:05:59.240
and look at where they got.

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:00.970
And we truly wanted people to heroes

00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:02.210
of their own stories.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:04.640
- I agree, and I think because
there is such a high rise

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:06.690
of just you know, all
these social platforms,

00:06:06.690 --> 00:06:08.950
that we lose human connection

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:11.510
and story and just examples

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:12.620
and Nicole and I were just like,

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:13.453
you know what?

00:06:13.453 --> 00:06:15.080
If there are people who've gone through

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:17.210
like you know, we had a really rough

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:20.410
childhood with our father
and just Nicole's experience

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:22.020
in high school and mine.

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:24.270
If there is people out there
who are doing it alone,

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:25.450
or at least our story is to let them know

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:28.190
that they're not alone and
that there is light at the end

00:06:28.190 --> 00:06:29.023
of the tunnel.
- Yeah.

00:06:29.023 --> 00:06:29.856
- Yeah.

00:06:29.856 --> 00:06:30.700
Hey, thank you guys.

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:33.340
Like, for one, being great examples

00:06:33.340 --> 00:06:35.610
for little girls and then also for

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:37.350
being that vulnerable,

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:38.880
'cause that's not an easy place to be

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:40.460
especially in the public eye.

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:43.290
So thank you so much
for hanging out with me

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:45.070
and congratulations.

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:46.650
Okay, we're gonna take a break,

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:48.427
but y'all the Bella
twins' new book is called

00:06:48.427 --> 00:06:50.660
"Incomparable" and it's
in stores right now

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:52.990
and you never know how it
can help you change your life

00:06:52.990 --> 00:06:54.590
and impact you, so check it out.

